19:T851,## 1. Clarify requirements (always do this first)

- **Browse / select** a product from the visible slots.
- **Accept coins** (or notes) until the price is covered.
- **Dispense** the item and **return change** for any overpayment.
- Handle the awkward cases: **sold-out** slots, and **cancel** → refund what was inserted.

State the assumptions out loud, it's half of what the interviewer is grading.

## 2. The naive boolean-flag mess

The first instinct is a pile of flags on one class:

```
boolean isSelecting, isPaid, isDispensing;
void insertCoin(int c) {
    if (isDispensing) return;           // ignore
    if (!isSelecting && !isPaid) { ... } // but which?
    balance += c;
    if (balance >= price) isPaid = true;
}
// …and insertCoin / select / dispense each re-check every flag
```

Every method re-derives "where am I?" from the same flags, illegal combos (`isPaid && isDispensing`) creep in, and adding a state means editing every method. It rots.

## 3. The State pattern

Make the machine a **Context** that delegates to a current **VMState**. Each state, `IdleState`, `HasMoney`, `Dispensing`handles `insertCoin()` / `selectProduct()` / `dispense()` **its own way** and decides the **next** state:

```
class VendingMachine {
    private VMState state = new IdleState(this);
    void insertCoin(Coin c) { state.insertCoin(c); }  // delegate
    void setState(VMState s) { this.state = s; }
}
```

Inserting a coin in `IdleState` is **legal**; pressing dispense in `IdleState` is **rejected by that state**. No scattered `if/else`each state polices itself.

## 4. Inventory + Product

Keep the data simple: an `Inventory` maps slot codes → `Product` (price + stock count). The states drive *behaviour*; the inventory holds the *what*. Sold-out is just a stock check the `HasMoney` state runs before moving on.

## 5. The transition diagram

Drawing the **state machine** (Idle → HasMoney → Dispensing → Idle, plus cancel) is the payoff: it's the spec, and it maps one-to-one onto the state classes. Adding "Maintenance" or "OutOfChange" is a new node **and** a new class, existing states untouched.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-case-studies","activeLesson":"vending-machine"}],["$","$L18","vending-machine",{"lesson":{"id":"vending-machine","patternId":"lld-case-studies","title":"Design a Vending Machine","kind":"case-study","difficulty":"Core","statement":"Select a product, insert coins, dispense the item, return change. The textbook use-case for modelling behaviour as a STATE machine instead of a tangle of flags.","companies":["Amazon","Microsoft","Flipkart"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"States as classes","code":["interface VMState { void insertCoin(Coin c); void select(Product p); }","class IdleState   implements VMState { ... }","class HasMoney    implements VMState { ... }","class Dispensing  implements VMState { ... }","class VendingMachine { VMState state; void insertCoin(c){ state.insertCoin(c); } }"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":5,"narration":"VendingMachine is the Context. It holds its CURRENT VMState and delegates every button press and coin straight to it, no flags of its own. Inventory just maps slots to products.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"vm","name":"VendingMachine","fields":["- state: VMState"],"methods":["+ insertCoin()","+ select(p)"],"x":0,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"state","name":"VMState","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ insertCoin()","+ select(p)","+ dispense()"],"x":1.4,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent2"},{"id":"inv","name":"Inventory","fields":["- slots: Map"],"x":2.6,"y":0.2},{"id":"idle","name":"IdleState","x":0,"y":1.55},{"id":"paid","name":"HasMoney","x":1,"y":1.55},{"id":"disp","name":"Dispensing","x":2,"y":1.55}],"relations":[{"id":"r1","from":"vm","to":"state","kind":"aggregate","label":"current"},{"id":"r2","from":"idle","to":"state","kind":"implement"},{"id":"r3","from":"paid","to":"state","kind":"implement"},{"id":"r4","from":"disp","to":"state","kind":"implement"}],"shownClassIds":["vm","state","inv"],"shownRelIds":["r1"],"activeIds":["vm"]},"vars":[["VendingMachine","delegates to state"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"Idle, HasMoney, and Dispensing each implement VMState. Each one knows what is legal right now and what state comes next, the behaviour lives in the state, not the machine.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["vm","state","inv","idle","paid","disp"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3","r4"],"activeIds":["idle","paid","disp"]}},{"view":"class","narration":"So inserting a coin in Idle is valid; pressing dispense in Idle is simply rejected by IdleState. No scattered if/else re-checking flags, each state polices itself, and adding a state is just one more class.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["vm","state","inv","idle","paid","disp"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3","r4"],"activeIds":[]},"vars":[["dispense() in Idle","rejected by IdleState ✓"],["add a state","= 1 class"]]}]},{"label":"The lifecycle","code":["class IdleState implements VMState {","    void insertCoin(Coin c){ vm.setState(new HasMoney(vm)); }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"state","codeLine":1,"narration":"The machine sits Idle, waiting. Whatever happens next is whatever the Idle state allows, everything else is ignored.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"paid","label":"HasMoney","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"disp","label":"Dispensing","x":2.5,"y":0.5}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"paid","label":"insertCoin()"},{"id":"e2","from":"paid","to":"disp","label":"select()"},{"id":"e3","from":"disp","to":"idle","label":"dispense()"},{"id":"e4","from":"paid","to":"idle","label":"cancel()"}],"activeId":"idle","firedEdgeId":"$undefined","label":"vending machine lifecycle"}},{"view":"state","codeLine":2,"narration":"Insert a coin: the Idle state handles it by moving the machine to HasMoney. It sets the next state itself.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"paid","label":"HasMoney","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"disp","label":"Dispensing","x":2.5,"y":0.5}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"paid","label":"insertCoin()"},{"id":"e2","from":"paid","to":"disp","label":"select()"},{"id":"e3","from":"disp","to":"idle","label":"dispense()"},{"id":"e4","from":"paid","to":"idle","label":"cancel()"}],"activeId":"paid","firedEdgeId":"e1","label":"vending machine lifecycle"},"vars":[["Idle.insertCoin()","→ HasMoney"]]},{"view":"state","narration":"Now in HasMoney, select() a product. If it is in stock, the HasMoney state moves the machine to Dispensing. (cancel() here would refund and drop back to Idle instead.)","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"paid","label":"HasMoney","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"disp","label":"Dispensing","x":2.5,"y":0.5}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"paid","label":"insertCoin()"},{"id":"e2","from":"paid","to":"disp","label":"select()"},{"id":"e3","from":"disp","to":"idle","label":"dispense()"},{"id":"e4","from":"paid","to":"idle","label":"cancel()"}],"activeId":"disp","firedEdgeId":"e2","label":"vending machine lifecycle"},"vars":[["HasMoney.select()","→ Dispensing"]]},{"view":"state","narration":"Dispensing drops the item and any change, then returns to Idle for the next customer. Each state owns its exits, adding \"OutOfChange\" is one node and one class, the rest untouched.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":0,"y":0.5,"kind":"start"},{"id":"paid","label":"HasMoney","x":1.25,"y":0.5},{"id":"disp","label":"Dispensing","x":2.5,"y":0.5}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"paid","label":"insertCoin()"},{"id":"e2","from":"paid","to":"disp","label":"select()"},{"id":"e3","from":"disp","to":"idle","label":"dispense()"},{"id":"e4","from":"paid","to":"idle","label":"cancel()"}],"activeId":"idle","firedEdgeId":"e3","label":"vending machine lifecycle"},"vars":[["add a state","= 1 class, no if/else ✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
